 Data Engineering Internship (London) 

 *NOTE - We accept students needing placements or otherwise extended internships. We also allow internships to take place during a non-summer term (for example - the winter, spring, or fall months) if preferable when it makes sense. &nbsp; 

 What you will do: 

 Our data engineering internship is an intensive 10-week experience with our team who&nbsp;is responsible for&nbsp;developing and&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;the infrastructure and pipelines to support data for firm wide&nbsp;use.&nbsp;You&nbsp;will be working side by side with our experienced data&nbsp;engineers&nbsp;and&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;receive ongoing feedback and coaching from a dedicated mentor throughout the summer. Our internship program is the primary way we&nbsp;identify&nbsp;top&nbsp;engineers&nbsp;and&nbsp;it’s&nbsp;a proven path for earning full-time opportunities at Jump. &nbsp; 

 You will take on projects working on production code and gain experience with our full-cycle process for development, testing, and release using Agile methodologies. You will apply your programming and analysis skills to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;and develop our firm wide data solutions. Other duties as assigned or needed. &nbsp; 

 Skills you will need: 
 Hands-on experience and&nbsp;a high level&nbsp;of&nbsp;proficiency&nbsp;in one or more of the following: &nbsp; 


 Python development on Linux platform &nbsp; 



 Strong understanding of data structures and threading models &nbsp; 



 Ability to work with a team in a fast-paced environment, deploying new software daily &nbsp; 



 Passion for solving complex problems and learning to build&nbsp;optimal&nbsp;solutions from scratch, instead of simply assembling things from existing libraries &nbsp; 



 Interest in using knowledge from several areas -- such as data pipelining and database management -- to ensure firm wide data integrity &nbsp; 



 Comfortability with Claude Code &nbsp; 



 Reliable and predictable availability &nbsp; 


 * No finance or economics study or work experience&nbsp;required &nbsp; 

 Also helpful, but not&nbsp;required: &nbsp; 


 Past internship or job experience in a data engineering role is a plus &nbsp; 



 Advanced coursework in algorithms&nbsp;&amp; data structures &nbsp; 

 Exposure to data analytics tools such as Pandas &nbsp; 


 INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS are encouraged to apply.&nbsp; &nbsp;

About Akuna &nbsp; 

 Akuna Capital is an innovative trading firm with a strong focus on collaboration,&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;technology, data-driven solutions, and automation. We specialize in providing liquidity on a variety of exchanges&nbsp;across various asset classes, primarily as&nbsp;an options market maker. To do this successfully, we&nbsp;build&nbsp;and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;our own low-latency technologies, including application frameworks, trading strategies, and mathematical models. &nbsp; 

 Our Founding Partners first conceptualized Akuna in their hometown of Sydney, Australia. They opened the firm’s first office in 2011 in the heart of the derivatives industry and the options capital of the world – Chicago. Today, Akuna is proud to&nbsp;operate&nbsp;from&nbsp;additional&nbsp;offices around the world:&nbsp;Sydney, Shanghai, Singapore, and London. &nbsp; 

 What&nbsp;you’ll&nbsp;do as a&nbsp;C++&nbsp;Software Engineer Intern at Akuna: &nbsp; &nbsp; 

 C++ software engineer&nbsp;interns at Akuna&nbsp;have the opportunity to&nbsp;work on a variety of high-performance systems that power the firm’s core business operations.&nbsp;Our&nbsp;interns are&nbsp;embedded&nbsp;on small-to-medium-sized teams that&nbsp;frequently&nbsp;interface with Quant and Trading, allowing them to&nbsp;focus on&nbsp;a specific domain area while&nbsp;still experiencing the day-to-day life of an Akuna software engineer. Akuna’s C++ systems are heavily multithreaded, asynchronous, and distributed by nature, which comes with a slew of challenges; our engineers are tasked with ensuring these systems are reliable, efficient, scalable, and flexible enough for even the most niche use cases.&nbsp; 

 Over their 10-week Akunacademy experience, software engineer interns will work on one or more valuable projects, progressing from ideation and design all the way to delivery and maintenance. These projects range from adding functionality onto existing systems to implementing brand new componentry to experimenting with new technologies and patterns to better understand the solution space. Akuna is looking for software engineer interns who are motivated, can solve complex problems, and are willing to reach for creative solutions when faced with novel problems. We value innovation, hard work, and knowledge, and we want our engineer interns to make a direct impact on the firm. Whether you are interested in algorithms and data structures, concurrency, networking and protocols, performance tuning, data capture and analysis, mathematical modeling, hardware, or something else, there’s engaging work to be done. &nbsp; 

 Requirements&nbsp;for This Role &nbsp; 


 Pursuing a bachelor’s,&nbsp;master’s, or&nbsp;Ph.D. in a technical field (computer science/engineering, math,&nbsp;physics, or equivalent) &nbsp; 



 Graduating&nbsp;by&nbsp;August 2028 &nbsp; 



 Legal authorization to work in the U.S. as of the first day of employment, including F-1 students using OPT or STEM &nbsp; 


 Previous&nbsp;experience in finance or trading is&nbsp; not &nbsp;required.&nbsp;Many of our&nbsp;engineers&nbsp;joined&nbsp;Akuna with little-to-no&nbsp;prior&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;of the markets, and we pride ourselves on our ability to onboard those new to the industry. Training and continuous education are provided for all engineers to ensure they can build&nbsp;the requisite technical and non-technical skillset for success. &nbsp; 

 Qualities That Make a Great C++ Software Engineer Candidate &nbsp; 


 Experience programming in modern C++ (C++20&nbsp;or later;&nbsp;C++23&nbsp;preferred) &nbsp; 



 Experience with several of the following &nbsp; 





 Distributed systems &nbsp; 








 Parallel processing &nbsp; 








 Asynchronous&nbsp;architectures &nbsp; 








 Networking or protocol encoding/decoding &nbsp; 








 Lock-free data structures and&nbsp;algorithms &nbsp; 








 Performance profiling (e.g.&nbsp;perf,&nbsp;gprof,&nbsp;vtune) &nbsp; 








 Scripting, such as in Python or&nbsp;shell &nbsp; 






 Familiarity with standard debugging tools&nbsp;(e.g.&nbsp;GDB,&nbsp;Valgrind, address sanitizer) &nbsp; 



 The ability to effectively communicate with non-technical stakeholders in Quant and Trading to obtain requirements, workshop solutions, and implement agreed-upon roadmaps &nbsp; 



 The ability to react quickly and effectively to rapidly changing market conditions, including the ability to quickly and accurately respond and/or solve math and coding problems, is an essential function of the role&nbsp; 



 A passion for&nbsp;building&nbsp;complex&nbsp;systems from the ground up &nbsp; 



 The ability to collaborate with other developers of&nbsp;different backgrounds, specialties, and knowledge levels to collectively deliver&nbsp;cohesive solutions to non-trivial problems &nbsp; 



 An intrinsically motivated attitude and the ability to work independently &nbsp; 



 A strong sense&nbsp;of ownership, including a drive to fix bugs when they inevitably arise &nbsp; 


 In addition to the above technical skills, Akuna&nbsp;values diversity of experience and perspective. We believe that&nbsp;engineers with&nbsp;varied backgrounds and interests allow&nbsp;us to&nbsp;approach problems from&nbsp;unique&nbsp;angles&nbsp;and&nbsp;to&nbsp;uncover innovative,&nbsp;optimal&nbsp;solutions.&nbsp;We want everyone to feel empowered to apply; we welcome your application, and we strongly encourage you to take the first steps in joining us&nbsp;in the future! &nbsp; 

 Resumes&nbsp; must &nbsp;be&nbsp;submitted&nbsp;in PDF format. &nbsp; 

 By applying to this role, you are&nbsp;indicating&nbsp;this is your top preference and acknowledge you will not be considered for other Quant and/or Tech roles at Akuna this recruiting season. This acknowledgement does not limit applications to Trading roles - in addition to this role, you may apply to any Trader roles of interest.

 We are an AI-friendly company and encourage employees to leverage AI in their daily work. However, AI assistance is not permitted during interviews or assessments . Our interview process is designed to evaluate your individual skills and judgment , and the use of AI tools will result in disqualification from the hiring process. 

 &nbsp; In accordance with&nbsp;the Illinois Equal Pay Act, the minimum base salary starts at $145,000. Exact compensation offered may vary based on many factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s experience, qualifications, and skill set. This role is also eligible for a discretionary performance bonus as part of the total compensation package and includes a comprehensive benefits package that may encompass employer-paid medical, dental, vision, retirement contributions, paid time off, and other benefits. The minimum base salary&nbsp;herein&nbsp;was&nbsp;determined&nbsp;in good faith by Akuna Capital LLC. &nbsp;
